# Three plural endings in Russian: -ам, -ами, -ах
subtitle: "Tom's first day in the kitchen: in the plural, every gender takes the same three endings, -ам, -ами and -ах, and adjectives follow."
tags: ["russian","russian plural cases","russian endings","russian grammar","kitchen"]
teaches: ["grammar/plural-cases","vocabulary/cooking","vocabulary/jobs"]
thumb: "band \"Three endings. Every gender.\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Across and past in Russian: перейти через, пройти мимо","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/107-russian-commute.cast"}

## Three plural endings in Russian: -ам, -ами, -ах
stress: all
shuffle: true
heading: false

